HST Office: a .docx export writes an OLE object's ProgID from the interop grab bag the import
filled, keyed by the object's name. Objects that come back from Undo (converted MathType equations
after Ctrl+Z, a deleted object restored) have new names, so they were written with ProgID="" and
Word and MathType no longer recognised them as MathType equations. When the grab bag has no
ProgID for an object, it is now read from the object's own stored compound file (its \1CompObj
stream; sw/source/filter/ww8/hst/hstoleprogid.cxx).
Test: CppunitTest_sw_uibase_uiview, testUndoneDeletionKeepsMathTypeProgID.

